{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-fundamental-object","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:fundamental-object","kind":"definition","title":"Fundamental object","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-rigid-monoidal-category"],"cites":["references/deligne1990"],"tags":["category-theory","fundamental-object","self-dual","tannaka-krein"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.FundamentalObject","text":"fundamental-object.md","leanSource":"fundamental-object.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:fundamental-object\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code> be an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-linear rigid <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-monoidal-category\">monoidal category</a>. A <strong>fundamental object</strong> is an object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V \\in \\mathbf{C}</code> equipped with a volume form</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\epsilon \\colon V \\otimes V \\longrightarrow \\mathbf{1}</code></pre>\n<p>— the categorical determinant <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Lambda^2 V \\to \\mathbf{1}</code> — together with an adjoint coform <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\eta \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to V \\otimes V</code> satisfying the two snake identities.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.md","heading":"Definition","number":"3.4.7","page":"b/def-fundamental-object","qa":{"counts":{"pass":71,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":8,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.FundamentalObject","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/fundamental-object.lean","compiles"